From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: khaliforce <kforce@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:00:45 +0900
Subject: pinctrl: sunxi: use a dynamic GPIO base

A fixed GPIO base is deprecated and gpiolib warns at boot:
"Static allocation of GPIO base is deprecated, use dynamic allocation."
Let gpiolib pick the base.

The global GPIO numbers in the legacy sysfs interface are no longer
fixed. The GPIO character device and device tree references do not
change.

Tested on MangoPi MQ Pro (D1).
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sunxi.c
@@ -1742,7 +1742,7 @@ int sunxi_pinctrl_init_with_flags(struct platform_device *pdev,
 			    pctl->desc->pin_base;
 	pctl->chip->label = dev_name(&pdev->dev);
 	pctl->chip->parent = &pdev->dev;
-	pctl->chip->base = pctl->desc->pin_base;
+	pctl->chip->base = -1;
 
 	ret = gpiochip_add_data(pctl->chip, pctl);
 	if (ret)
-- 
